#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# numeric_array

#% text
# `numeric_array(xs, type)` is the array `xs` of numbers stored in the machine type `type`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The types are `"Integer8"`, `"Integer16"`, `"Integer32"`, `"Integer64"`, `"UnsignedInteger8"`, ..., `"Real32"`, `"Real64"`, `"ComplexReal32"` and `"ComplexReal64"`.

#% item
# The object stays unevaluated; `normal(numeric_array(xs, type))` gives the list back, with the entries of an integer type kept to its range (`clip_and_coerce` as a third argument clips to the range, `round` rounds first) and those of a real type as machine reals (single-precision rounding of `"Real32"` is not applied).

#% item
# A conversion is a numeric array of the converted values: `numeric_array(xs, type, clip_and_coerce)` (or `round`), and a numeric array or `byte_array` given a type again, become `numeric_array(values, type)`; a real type gets machine reals (for `"Real32"` clipped to its range by `clip_and_coerce`).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
numeric_array([1, 2, 3, 4], "Real32")
#% output
#= numeric_array([1, 2, 3, 4], "Real32")

#% cell
numeric_array([[1, 2], [3, 4]], "UnsignedInteger8")
#% output
#= numeric_array([[1, 2], [3, 4]], "UnsignedInteger8")

#% cell
normal(numeric_array([0, 1, 2], "UnsignedInteger8"))
#% output
#= [0, 1, 2]

#% cell
normal(numeric_array([0, 1000, 2000], "UnsignedInteger8", clip_and_coerce))
#% output
#= [0, 255, 255]

#% cell
normal(numeric_array([0.1, 1.1, 2.1], "UnsignedInteger8", round))
#% output
#= [0, 1, 2]

#% cell
numeric_array(numeric_array([-100, 0, 5, 120], "Integer8"), "UnsignedInteger8", clip_and_coerce)
#% output
#= numeric_array([0, 0, 5, 120], "UnsignedInteger8")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `normal`, `array_reshape`
